Fix a real upstream per-model gap (not an AXOS feature, and the same
category the original 0a1cab5/3897483 prebuild audit was checking for —
this one slipped through it): router/Makefile's `obj-y += asd2.1` builds
the asd2.1 security daemon unconditionally for every model. asd2.1/Makefile's
own build step already tolerates a model with no
asd2.1/prebuild/$(BUILD_NAME)/{asd,libasd.so} — its prebuild copy uses a
leading "-" to ignore a missing file. No such prebuild exists for GT-AX6000
(confirmed: asd2.1/prebuild/ only has entries for GT-AXE11000, RT-AX68U,
RT-AX88U, RT-AX58U, RT-AX86U, and GT-AX11000). The original prebuild audit
(see build.sh's comments) noted this exact leniency and concluded asd2.1 was
"not a risk" — but that only covers asd2.1's own build step; the separate
`asd2.1-install` target in router/Makefile does not have the same leniency.

Confirmed via a real build attempt: `make gt-ax6000` fails with "install:
cannot stat 'asd2.1/asd': No such file or directory" once GT-AX6000's
absent prebuild leaves nothing for asd2.1's build step to produce either.

Fix: add the same leading "-" (ignore-errors) to the two `install -D` lines
and the two (already RTCONFIG_DEBUG-conditional) strip lines in
`asd2.1-install`, matching the leniency this codebase already established
for this exact scenario in asd2.1/Makefile itself.

`git apply --check`-verified against the pinned tag (3004.388.9), applied on
top of 0001-0011. Not yet verified past that point in a completed build —
see docs/build-environment.md and docs/ROADMAP.md.

diff --git a/release/src/router/Makefile b/release/src/router/Makefile
index fe6950ea62..825e60d787 100644
--- a/release/src/router/Makefile
+++ b/release/src/router/Makefile
@@ -8615,11 +8640,20 @@ asd-clean:
 asd2.1: shared $(if $(BCM_502L07P2),ethctl_lib) nvram$(BCMEX)$(EX7) curl openssl libasc
 	$(MAKE) -C $@
 
+# asd2.1/Makefile's own build step already tolerates a model with no
+# asd2.1/prebuild/$(BUILD_NAME)/{asd,libasd.so} (its prebuild copy uses a
+# leading "-" to ignore a missing file — see asd2.1/Makefile) — no such
+# prebuild exists for GT-AX6000. This install step did not have the same
+# leniency: confirmed via a real build attempt, "install: cannot stat
+# 'asd2.1/asd': No such file or directory" once GT-AX6000's absent
+# prebuild left nothing for asd2.1's own build step to produce either.
+# Matched the leniency this codebase already established for this exact
+# per-model gap.
 asd2.1-install:
-	install -D asd2.1/asd $(INSTALLDIR)/asd2.1/usr/bin/asd
-	install -D asd2.1/libasd.so $(INSTALLDIR)/asd2.1/usr/lib/libasd.so
-	$(if $(RTCONFIG_DEBUG),,$(STRIP) $(INSTALLDIR)/asd2.1/usr/bin/asd)
-	$(if $(RTCONFIG_DEBUG),,$(STRIP) $(INSTALLDIR)/asd2.1/usr/lib/libasd.so)
+	-install -D asd2.1/asd $(INSTALLDIR)/asd2.1/usr/bin/asd
+	-install -D asd2.1/libasd.so $(INSTALLDIR)/asd2.1/usr/lib/libasd.so
+	$(if $(RTCONFIG_DEBUG),,-$(STRIP) $(INSTALLDIR)/asd2.1/usr/bin/asd)
+	$(if $(RTCONFIG_DEBUG),,-$(STRIP) $(INSTALLDIR)/asd2.1/usr/lib/libasd.so)
 
 asd2.1-clean:
 	$(MAKE) -C asd2.1 clean
